    "result_text": "All 65 tests pass \u2014 **BUILD SUCCESS**, no regressions.\n\n## What I did\n\nThe `POST /api/owners` pipeline already emitted a human-readable audit line (`AuditOwnerCreated`). I added the structured event as a separate, single-responsibility pipeline step so the existing line is untouched.\n\n**New function class** \u2014 `src/main/java/.../rest/function/owner/AuditOwnerCreatedEvent.java`:\n- Emits an immutable `OwnerCreatedEvent` record as JSON on the same `AUDIT` logger:\n  `{\"seq\":1,\"ownerId\":11,\"customerCode\":\"NSW-16E6609E\",\"membershipLevel\":1,\"event\":\"OWNER_CREATED\"}`\n- `seq` is a process-wide `AtomicLong`, monotonically increasing across every create (not reset by per-request transaction rollback).\n- Serialized with the injected Jackson 3 `ObjectMapper` bean; field order in the record fixes the JSON order.\n\n**Handling the \"primary identifier\" evolution note:** the identifier is pulled through a single `primaryIdentifier(owner)` method that currently returns `owner.getCustomerCode()`. That's the one place that changes when the customerCode is later unified into the memberId \u2014 the event will then carry the memberId with no other rewiring. The record field and that method are the only edit points.\n\n**Pipeline wiring** \u2014 `owners.POST.yml`: inserted an `auditEvent` step (under `govern: [ transaction ]`) between `audit` and `recordIdempotency`, so it runs after `save` (owner has its id) and after `assignCode`/`assignMembership*` (identifier and level are populated).\n\nThe driving test `Cp53Tests` now passes, as do the pre-existing audit tests `Cp21`/`Cp43` and the full suite.",
